  "source": {
    "title": "Fermanagh Herald, 20 May 1961, p. 5 (\"New Enniskillen Borough Council\")",
    "publisher": "Fermanagh Herald (via the Irish Newspaper Archives)",
    "kind": "news",
    "check": "six aldermen and fifteen councillors, twenty-one members in all, returned unopposed; no wards or votes printed.",
    "url": "https://irishnewsarchive.com/?a=d&d=FMH19610520.1.5"
  },
  "note": "Municipal elections, 17 May 1961; the borough council was elected without a contest, the councillors for three years and the aldermen for six. The paper lists the six aldermen first (McKeown, O'Hare, Bryson, George Elliott, Burnside, Barton) and then the fifteen councillors, by party but not by ward. It states the whole council was elected 'without a contest'. The seven Nationalists (McKeown, O'Hare, H. Morris, Leo Quinn, J. J. Donnelly, J. Lunny, M. R. Donnelly) are the North Ward members named in the Irish News, 3 May 1961, p. 3; the paper does not allocate the fourteen Unionists between East and South Wards, so they are recorded together. Returned unopposed."
}
